  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-wrap: break-word; text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-c26a34bb-1cfd-48ec-8205-e6c43c88a41a-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 5px; border: none;">
<h2 style="text-align: center; line-height: 1.2; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 18px;" align="center">City of Columbus Pre-kindergarten Initiative</h2>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Mayor Andrew J. Ginther’s vision for America’s Opportunity City is universal access to a high-quality pre-kindergarten education for every 4-year-old in Columbus.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Established by the city in 2014, Early Start Columbus (ESC) awards grants to community-based providers to help increase the number of children who enter kindergarten ready to learn.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">If your center is located within Franklin County, is in good standing with all licensing bodies and held at least a three-star rating under Step Up To Quality, Ohio’s Tiered Quality Rating and Improvement System, during the 2023-2024 school year, <strong>we invite you to submit a letter of intent to apply for funding for the 2024-2025 school year</strong>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Children served must be four years old by September 30, 2024 and reside within the boundaries of the City of Columbus. Pre-kindergarten services must be offered for a full day (five hours of instruction per day, exclusive of before and after care, recesses and breakfast/lunch periods) and for the school year (approximately 850 hours). The family income of children served must be no more than 300% of the Federal Poverty Level (FPL).</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">The Mayor's Office of Education will braid Publicly Funded Child Care (ODJFS) and Early Childhood Education grant (ODE) to award funding for the expansion of high-quality pre-kindergarten education for the 2024-2025 school year. Providers should apply for and, if awarded, accept Publicly Funded Child Care. Similarly, providers should accept the Ohio Department of Education’s Early Childhood Education grant. Early Start Columbus funds should be considered last-dollar grants.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Reimbursement rates range from $850-$10,000 per child per year depending on income eligibility, other funding sources available (Publicly Funded Child Care and Early Childhood Education grant) and the program’s star rating.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Please submit your letter of intent to apply, along with your applicant funding request worksheet </strong>with the amount of your request to <a href="https://agency.e-cimpact.com/login.aspx?org=37145F&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">https://agency.e-cimpact.com/login.aspx?org=37145F</a>, b<strong>y April 19, 2024</strong>. Application materials for the 2024-2025 school year will be sent to you upon receipt of your letter of intent to apply.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">We look forward to partnering with you to help expand pre-kindergarten opportunities for our Columbus children. If you have any questions, please feel free to email us at <a href="mailto:education@columbus.gov" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">education@columbus.gov</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"> </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Sincerely,</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Mayor's Office of Education</p>
